</tr>
<tr>
<td>11</td>
<td>Do a quick test — say <em>&quot;Psalm 23:1&quot;</em> into the microphone</td>
<td>☐</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>12</td>
<td>Verify the verse appears in the Staging Queue</td>
<td>☐</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>13</td>
<td>Click <strong>PUSH LIVE</strong> and verify it appears in Holyrics/vMix</td>
<td>☐</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<h3>During the Service</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Watch the Staging Queue</strong> for detected scriptures and songs</li>
<li><strong>Click PUSH LIVE</strong> on each card when you&#39;re ready to display it</li>
<li>Use the <strong>Bible tab (Ctrl + B)</strong> to manually find and push specific verses</li>
<li>Use the <strong>Lyrics tab (Ctrl + L)</strong> to browse and push saved song lyrics</li>
<li>Use <strong>Arrow Keys</strong> to navigate between sections in lyric cards</li>
<li>Click <strong>CLEAR SCREEN</strong> when you want to remove the current display</li>
</ul>
<h3>After the Service</h3>
<ul>
<li>Click <strong>⏹ End Session</strong> if you started a recording session</li>
<li>Click <strong>🎙️ Audio: OFF</strong> to stop listening</li>
<li>Log out or simply close the browser tab</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>10. Troubleshooting &amp; FAQ {#troubleshooting}</h2>
<h3>&quot;Nothing is happening in vMix when I push a verse&quot;</h3>
<p><strong>Cause:</strong> Chrome is blocking the connection due to Mixed Content security.</p>
<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Click the padlock icon in the address bar → Site Settings → Insecure Content → Allow</li>
<li>Refresh the page with Ctrl + Shift + R</li>
<li>Try pushing again</li>
</ol>
<h3>&quot;Holyrics says Unauthorized&quot;</h3>
<p><strong>Cause:</strong> The API token in Corpus Engine doesn&#39;t match the one in Holyrics.</p>
<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Open Holyrics → File → Settings → API/Web tab</li>
<li>Copy the Token very carefully (no extra spaces)</li>
<li>Paste it into Corpus Engine&#39;s Settings → Holyrics Token field</li>
<li>Save and try again</li>
</ol>
<h3>&quot;The microphone is not picking up audio&quot;</h3>
<p><strong>Cause:</strong> Chrome&#39;s microphone permission may have been denied or reset.</p>
<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Click the padlock icon in the address bar → Site Settings</li>
<li>Find <strong>Microphone</strong> and set it to <strong>Allow</strong></li>
<li>Refresh the page and click Audio: ON again</li>
</ol>
<h3>&quot;The text is getting cut off in vMix&quot;</h3>
<p><strong>Cause:</strong> The vMix Title text box doesn&#39;t have Auto Shrink or Word Wrap enabled.</p>
<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Open the <strong>GT Title Designer</strong> application (search for it in the Windows Start menu)</li>
<li>Open your title template (File → Open)</li>
<li>Click the <strong>Headline</strong> layer on the right side</li>
<li>Go to the <strong>Home</strong> tab and check <strong>Auto Shrink</strong> and <strong>Word Wrap</strong></li>
<li>Save the file and reload it in vMix</li>
</ol>
<h3>&quot;Scriptures are not being detected&quot;</h3>
<p><strong>Cause:</strong> Audio might not be reaching the system, or the AI engine might be off.</p>
<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Make sure <strong>Audio: ON</strong> is toggled (you should see it highlighted green)</li>
<li>Make sure <strong>AI: ON</strong> is toggled for paraphrased scriptures</li>
<li>Speak clearly into the microphone</li>
<li>If using an external audio source (mixing desk), make sure the AUX output is connected</li>
</ol>
<h3>&quot;Songs are not found when I search&quot;</h3>
<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Use the format: <strong>&quot;Song Title - Artist Name&quot;</strong> (e.g., <em>&quot;Way Maker - Sinach&quot;</em>)</li>
<li>If the song is very new or regional, it might not be in the lyrics database. You can manually type and save lyrics.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
